        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0566" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg460"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Sleeper to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 30, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 164.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report to the
                    department that complaint has been made to this legation, through the Cienfuegos
                    consulate, by the following American companies, seeking protection for their
                    rights and property:</p>
                <p>The Colonial Sugars Company, (Constancia), Mr. R. B. Childs. The Hormiguero
                    Central Company, of Hormiguero. The Trinidad Plantation, Mr. S. M. Patterson.
                    The Cuba Cattle and Land Company, Trinidad, Mr. H. S. Ismon.</p>
                <p>Immediately upon receipt of this complaint, I addressed a note to the foreign
                    office, copy herewith inclosed, requesting the necessary protection.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacob Sleeper</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d399-a1.xml" xpointer="d399-a1"/>
            </div>
